  "reason": "The current best is config_010 (pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) at 0.639 accuracy. Key evidence: (1) avgpool >> transformer (0.639 vs 0.573), (2) weighted >> concat (0.639 vs 0.619), (3) pca_n2000 >> scgpt (0.639 vs 0.525), and (4) resnet50 ≈ imagenet_vit_l (0.639 vs 0.635). The one major untested variable in the best-known architecture is the RNA encoder scvi_n200. config_035 isolates this single change (scvi_n200 replacing pca_n2000) while holding all other settings at their proven-best values. This is critical because scgpt was a different learned encoder that performed poorly, but scvi_n200 (a VAE-based 200-dim representation) is architecturally distinct and untested. If it improves, we have a new best; if not, we can confidently rule out learned RNA encoders and focus remaining budget on other axes. Expected relative cost: moderate, roughly 10–11 GPU hours (similar to config_010's 10.60 hrs since it uses the same resnet50 image encoder and multiprofile avgpool architecture, with a slightly smaller RNA representation)."
}

